WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.138
<v Senior Eligibility Worker>I put a lot into that tips sheet. I have

00:00:03.138 --> 00:00:06.276
<v Senior Eligibility Worker>taken calls from these communities for twenty years. The patterns

00:00:06.276 --> 00:00:08.472
<v Senior Eligibility Worker>are real. New staff walk in blind.

00:00:08.822 --> 00:00:13.216
<v Human Services Supervisor>I believe the patterns are real. I also read a

00:00:13.216 --> 00:00:17.611
<v Human Services Supervisor>meta-analysis of 558 studies. About 80 percent of the variation

00:00:17.611 --> 00:00:21.566
<v Human Services Supervisor>in work values was inside countries, not between them.

00:00:21.916 --> 00:00:24.244
<v Senior Eligibility Worker>So you are saying my experience is wrong?

00:00:24.594 --> 00:00:28.341
<v Human Services Supervisor>No. I am saying it describes the range, not the

00:00:28.341 --> 00:00:32.087
<v Human Services Supervisor>person. Your sheet says some callers say yes to be

00:00:32.087 --> 00:00:35.834
<v Human Services Supervisor>polite. That is true for some. For the caller last

00:00:35.834 --> 00:00:38.082
<v Human Services Supervisor>week, nobody knows, because nobody asked.

00:00:38.432 --> 00:00:41.187
<v Senior Eligibility Worker>Fair. The new worker assumed the yes meant no and

00:00:41.187 --> 00:00:43.942
<v Senior Eligibility Worker>closed the call. That was not what I meant the

00:00:43.942 --> 00:00:44.768
<v Senior Eligibility Worker>sheet to do.

00:00:45.118 --> 00:00:49.016
<v Human Services Supervisor>That is the risk. There are experiments on this. People

00:00:49.016 --> 00:00:52.914
<v Human Services Supervisor>told to imagine another person's view got no more accurate.

00:00:52.914 --> 00:00:56.422
<v Human Services Supervisor>Sometimes less. The only thing that helped was asking.

00:00:56.772 --> 00:00:58.908
<v Senior Eligibility Worker>Then what do new staff do with what I know?

00:00:59.258 --> 00:01:02.665
<v Human Services Supervisor>Your knowledge becomes the reason for the question. If some

00:01:02.665 --> 00:01:06.072
<v Human Services Supervisor>people decide with family, the worker asks who should be

00:01:06.072 --> 00:01:09.478
<v Human Services Supervisor>involved. If yes can mean many things, the worker does

00:01:09.478 --> 00:01:12.885
<v Human Services Supervisor>a read-back: what will you do next, and by what

00:01:12.885 --> 00:01:13.226
<v Human Services Supervisor>date?

00:01:13.576 --> 00:01:17.728
<v Senior Eligibility Worker>And language? Half the confusion I see is really language.

00:01:18.078 --> 00:01:22.345
<v Human Services Supervisor>That is the part with the strongest evidence. A review

00:01:22.345 --> 00:01:26.613
<v Human Services Supervisor>of 28 studies found professional interpreters beat family members and

00:01:26.613 --> 00:01:30.880
<v Human Services Supervisor>untrained staff. So the sheet should say: offer a professional

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:31.734
<v Human Services Supervisor>interpreter early.

00:01:32.084 --> 00:01:35.305
<v Senior Eligibility Worker>I can rewrite it. Each pattern, then the question it

00:01:35.305 --> 00:01:38.204
<v Senior Eligibility Worker>leads to. Then a date, never the word soon.

00:01:38.554 --> 00:01:41.017
<v Human Services Supervisor>Would you lead the practice session with the team? They

00:01:41.017 --> 00:01:43.234
<v Human Services Supervisor>will listen to you more than to a study.
